# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Constantia — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED TO RUN THE SITE.
# Without Firebase credentials the app falls back to the committed seed content
# in `src/lib/data/`, which is a complete, working dataset. `npm run dev` and
# `npm run build` both succeed with this file absent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Firebase Admin (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Only needed to read live content from Firestore at build time, or to run the
# seed/import scripts in `scripts/`. Supply ONE of the following.
#
# Never commit the credential file. Keep it outside the repository entirely.

# Path to a service account JSON file (simplest for local work):
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH=D:\keys\constantia.json

# Or the JSON inline (useful in CI):
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account", ...}

# Or the same JSON, base64 encoded:
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_BASE64=

# Or Google's standard variable:
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=D:\keys\constantia.json

# Overrides — both default correctly, set only if you use a different project.
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=constantia-agency
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=constantia-agency.firebasestorage.app


# --- Chatbot (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Used by src/app/api/chat/route.ts.
#
# NOTE: the site builds with `output: 'export'` (static). API routes are NOT
# included in the exported build, so this route does not run in production as
# currently configured. See README "Known issues".
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
